From 22cb9c4efa9a4d08d00da127cce1228500a52752 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 03:41:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(design-system): add 5 domain status adapters, integrate
 into caregiver UI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 4 of the status badge standardization. Rebased on ab2ba4b ('fix: batch
fix while waiting for uptime') per the pre-flight instruction — every file
in the hotfix reference list was re-read from that commit before editing;
none of its behaviors (extended relative-time formatting, CaregiverAlertMetric
.system handling, tab-lifecycle/optimistic-seen logic) are touched or reverted
here.

Adapters (lib/design_system/status/adapters/), each a thin StatelessWidget
plus a static describe() returning the raw AleraStatusDescriptor for reuse
with AleraBadgedAvatar:

- AlertSeverityChip: CaregiverAlertSeverity has only {warning, critical} —
  no info state exists in the domain model, despite the original 3-tone plan.
- ReminderStatusChip: CaregiverReminderStatus has only {missed, upcoming,
  completed} — no separate overdue/snoozed state. Added a missing
  reminderMissed label; 'missed' was incorrectly going to reuse 'Overdue'.
- DeviceStatusChip: connection (PatientDeviceConnectionStatus, which does
  have ) and battery (a raw percent) are independent in the data
  model. Low battery overrides 'Connected' only when actually connected, at
  or below a 20%-default, overridable threshold; a disconnected device's
  battery reading never overrides its offline state.
- PatientStatusChip: maps CareStatus (health/monitoring status), not
  PatientAccessState (account connection) — the original plan's 'Patient
  State' domain (Active/Pending Access/Inactive) is access state and remains
  unbuilt; this adapter answers a different question under the name the
  Patch 4 directive used. warning/needsAttention share a tone, split by
  icon+label.
- VitalTrendChip: VitalTrendSeverity only carries magnitude (info/warning/
  critical), not direction. Added a local VitalTrendDirection enum (not a
  backend concept) so a call site with the actual reading and the patient's
  normal range can supply direction; omitting it renders a direction-neutral
  fallback rather than guessing. critical-high get distinct labels from
  warning-high (High vs Elevated), and critical-low from warning-low
  (Critically low vs Low), so tone is never the only distinguishing signal.

Feature integration:
- CareRecipientCard (patient list, a genuine multi-patient feed): initials-only
  CircleAvatar -> AleraBadgedAvatar carrying CareStatus; ad hoc
  stable/'High Heart Rate' text row -> PatientStatusChip driven by the typed
  enum instead of a string fallback.
- CaregiverAlertCard: added AleraBadgedAvatar (radius 18, so the badge's 14px
  floor lands at ~39% of avatar diameter rather than overwhelming a smaller
  avatar) next to the patient name in the showPatientName branch, and an
  AlertSeverityChip under the title so severity is never colour-stripe-only.
- caregiver_shell.dart patient switcher: CircleAvatar+initials ->
  AleraBadgedAvatar with the patient's CareStatus; removed the now-unused
  _patientInitials helper.
- caregiver_alerts_page.dart's AlertListCard (defined, currently unused by any
  call site): _InitialAvatar -> AleraBadgedAvatar, for when it is wired up.

Updated test/features/caregiver/people/caregiver_people_page_test.dart:
'High Heart Rate' was an arbitrary placeholder for any non-stable status with
no tie to Maria Santos's actual CareStatus.needsAttention (confirmed against
the mock fixture); PatientStatusChip now renders 'Attention needed', the
correct label for her real status. Widened the card-height assertion since
the new status chip has more vertical padding than the plain text row it
replaced — flagged inline to confirm the exact number with a real test run.

Barrel: exported all 5 adapters from status.dart.

Tests: one file per adapter covering every enum value's tone/label/icon,
tone-sharing-but-label/icon-differing pairs (PatientStatusChip
warning/needsAttention, VitalTrendChip's four warning/critical x direction
combinations), the device battery-override interaction and its threshold
override, and labelOverride pass-through.
